      "settings": {
        "hasLoop": true,
        "query": {
          "objectType": "post",
          "post_type": [
            "location"
          ],
          "posts_per_page": "12",
          "orderby": "title",
          "order": "ASC"
        },
        "_cssGlobalClasses": [
          "y6j9lp",
          "cc161e",
          "cb8f51",
          "c27e53"
        ]
      },
      "label": "Query loop over the location CPT — own location-card__* class family (was a verbatim copy of service-card__* in the prior build; locations and services are different content per Crown_Movers_Content_Architecture_Spec_v2.md rule #3 — \"Physical branches and service areas are different things and never share a content type, a template, or a schema block\" — the card system shouldn't share one either). Not yet grouped by region (design brief: \"organize location links into clear regions, searchable groups, or expandable directories\") — each card shows its region as a label below, but the listing itself is still one flat loop; grouping into per-region sections is a reasonable next pass, deliberately not attempted here to avoid an unverified nested-query-loop pattern (region as outer loop, location filtered by the outer loop's current term) shipping untested."
    },
